WEBVTT

00:02:56.538 --> 00:03:00.496
Meanwhile, stress hormones affect 
immune cells in a variety of ways.

00:03:00.538 --> 00:03:04.704
Initially, they help prepare to fight 
invaders and heal after injury,

00:03:04.746 --> 00:03:08.704
but chronic stress can dampen 
the function of some immune cells,

00:03:08.746 --> 00:03:13.663
make you more susceptible to infections, 
and slow the rate you heal.

00:03:15.329 --> 00:03:16.746
Want to live a long life?

00:03:16.788 --> 00:03:19.246
You may have to curb your chronic stress.

00:03:19.288 --> 00:03:22.579
That’s because it has even been 
associated with shortened telomeres,

00:03:22.621 --> 00:03:26.121
the shoelace tip ends of chromosomes 
that measure a cell’s age.

00:03:26.163 --> 00:03:27.829
Telomeres cap chromosomes

00:03:27.871 --> 00:03:30.954
to allow DNA to get copied 
every time a cell divides